---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ClientCaseStudy from '../../../components/ClientCaseStudy.astro';
import { courseSync } from '../../../data/work';

// The StudyPro, a named client project, EN twin of /de/arbeiten/make-kursanmeldungen.
// Copy = make-work drafts/route6-named-page.md as approved by Christo 2026-10-26.
// Her system is described only through what she published; the review is quoted
// word for word from her Make Community post (t/111598 post 18).
const lang = 'en' as const;
const reviewUrl =
  'https://community.make.com/t/hiring-make-com-specialist-with-mindbody-api-experience/111598/18';
---

<Layout
  lang={lang}
  pageKey="arbeiten"
  title="Make.com automations for The StudyPro · 9592 Solutions"
  description="Make.com automations built for The StudyPro, a tutoring and enrichment business in Virginia: MindBody course purchases flowing into HubSpot, roster entries and drafted confirmation emails."
>
  <ClientCaseStudy
    lang={lang}
    study={courseSync}
    title="Make.com automations for The StudyPro: from MindBody course purchases to HubSpot, class rosters and parent emails"
    subtitle="Built for Debbie Rosen's tutoring and enrichment business in McLean and Reston, Virginia, and running in The StudyPro's own Make account."
    reviewUrl={reviewUrl}
    reviewBy="Debbie, The StudyPro"
  >
    <Fragment slot="starting">
      <p>
        The StudyPro sells multi-session courses through MindBody and keeps its families in HubSpot. In July 2026 Debbie Rosen posted a hiring request on the Make Community forum with a paid test project. When a student buys a course, the student's HubSpot contact should be updated, the student added to the right segment and the roster sheet, a VA alerted when there's a follow-up step, and a confirmation sent to the family. Within a few days I had built a working version of her specification on invented data and emailed it to her, and that became the pilot.
      </p>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="runs">
      <p>
        Her course registration automation is live. When a family books a course in MindBody, Make updates the family's HubSpot segment, adds the student to the roster sheet, alerts her VA when there's a follow-up step, and drafts the confirmation email. Since then the work has grown into other parts of how her team runs, including staff offboarding.
      </p>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="how">
      <p>
        Everything runs in The StudyPro's own Make account with its own connections, so the scenarios belong to the business and not to me. I test each build before it goes live.
      </p>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="review">
      <p>Quick update for anyone who finds this thread: we hired Christo Wilken, and I'm glad we did.</p>
      <p>We talked to five candidates. Christo stood out because he sent a working demo up front and was transparent about his approach and pricing from day one. Our course registration automation is now live: when a family books a course in MindBody, Make handles the HubSpot segment, adds them to our roster sheet, alerts our VA when there's a follow-up step, and drafts the confirmation email. That used to be a pile of manual steps for our front desk every time someone registered.</p>
      <p>He's now helping with our staff offboarding automation too. Highly recommend.</p>
    </Fragment>
  </ClientCaseStudy>
</Layout>
